Z||000000||Jim51||07-11-2000||05:20 PM||||I have a 87 coupe 2.5L 5 spd. I'm changing the slave cyclinder. The one I got from PEP Boys is shorter than the one that was in the car. The piston does not reach the clutch control arm. Has someone moved the arm to fit the longer slave cyclinder? What is the angle the arm should correctly be at? Mine is at 90 degress to the piston. Can it be adjusted? Or is the arm keyed into the clutch fork?||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||07-12-2000||11:22 AM||||I think you got the wrong slave. That is the slave for the getrag.<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fi.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000002||StuGood||07-12-2000||12:42 PM||||Well, that kind of explains something I saw in a used Fiero for sale a few years back.  It was a four-cylinder model, and it seemed to drive okay.  When I looked at the slave cylinder, saw a little chrome SOCKET wedged in between slave rod and the clutch lever!  Seller had just had a clutch installed by a "professional,"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> so I didn't say anything to the guy about it, but I thought, "What a kluge!"  Thanked him for showing me his car, and was on my way.<P>Needless to say, I don't think it's a good idea to do this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!     ||||reg||10
